Q: What is the Euler system for?
A: The Euler system is designed for solving difficult optimization problems involving programs. Specifically, it aims to find an input \( x \) to a function \( P \) written in a standard C-like language, such that the output \( P(x) \) is minimized with respect to an appropriate distance measure on the space of outputs of \( P \). This system is particularly useful for framing many problems in software engineering as optimization questions.
