- Adaptive concretization is designed to be more efficient and scalable by dynamically adjusting the search strategy based on the characteristics of the unknowns, whereas sketching typically follows a more uniform approach without this level of adaptability.

In summary, adaptive concretization enhances the sketching process by introducing a more nuanced and efficient method of searching for solutions, particularly in parallel computing environments.
